  "generated_text": "To find the constant term in the expansion of \\((x^4 + x + 5)(x^5 + x^3 + 15)\\), we need to identify the terms that will result in a constant term when multiplied together.\n\nFirst, let's identify the constant terms in each polynomial:\n- The constant term in \\(x^4 + x + 5\\) is \\(5\\).\n- The constant term in \\(x^5 + x^3 + 15\\) is \\(15\\).\n\nNext, we multiply these constant terms together:\n\\[\n5 \\times 15 = 75\n\\]\n\nThus, the constant term in the expansion of \\((x^4 + x + 5)(x^5 + x^3 + 15)\\) is \\(\\boxed{75}\\).",
